---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The spikes of one plan, as a plan graph: the writer of the brief of what they will
  measure, which never waits on them, the spikes the draft adds, and `finalize`, which
  reworks the plan from their reports and depends on every spike, as the draft adds each
  with its edge. The draft creates it as `<plan>-spikes` only when the plan needs a
  measurement, and the planning and finishing runs' `spikes` step launches it in the same
  flow. A launch redoes each spike whose task changed since it ran, and finalize behind it.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan whose spikes these are, `authoring:<native id>`.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id.
    type: text
    required: true
members:
  - id: "{{ native }}-spikes-brief"
    title: "Write the spike brief of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: spike-brief.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spike-brief
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/spike-brief.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/spike-brief.yaml
  - id: "{{ native }}-spikes-finalize"
    title: "Finalize {{ plan }} from its spikes"
    template: {file: finalize.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: finalize
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/planner.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/planner.yaml
---
The spikes of `{{ plan }}`: the spike brief's writer and each spike, run side by side, and
`finalize` behind every spike.
